.subckt TELESCOPIC VSS VDD VOUT VIP VIN IBIAS
* =====================================================================
* Telescopic cascode OTA — SKY130A (iteration 2)
* Sizing chosen for STRONG INVERSION (Vov ≈ 150 mV) to maximize gm·ro
* and avoid weak-inversion gain collapse.
* =====================================================================

* ---- IBIAS device (just for connectivity) ---------------------------
XM8     IBIAS  IBIAS  VSS    VSS  sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8  L=1 W=2 nf=1 m=1

* ---- IDEAL Tail current source (100 uA) -----------------------------
ITAIL   ntail  VSS    dc 100u

* ---- Input pair (NMOS, 50 uA each, strong inversion)
* For Vov ≈ 150 mV: W/L = 50uA/(0.5*100uA·0.0225) ≈ 44.
* W=4 nf=2 L=0.5 → W/L = 16. Too small. Try W=4 nf=4 L=0.5 → W/L=32. Vov~180mV. Good.
XM1     nd1    VIP    ntail  VSS  sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8  L=0.5 W=4 nf=4 m=1
XM2     nd2    VIN    ntail  VSS  sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8  L=0.5 W=4 nf=4 m=1

* ---- NMOS cascodes (LONG L for high ro)
XM3     na     Vb1    nd1    VSS  sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8  L=2 W=4 nf=4 m=1
XM4     VOUT   Vb1    nd2    VSS  sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8  L=2 W=4 nf=4 m=1

* ---- PMOS cascode (output side only, matched to mirror)
XM5     VOUT   Vb2    nb     VDD  sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8  L=2 W=8 nf=2 m=1

* ---- PMOS current mirror (1:1, LONG L for high ro)
* For PMOS at 50 uA, Vov ≈ 150 mV: W/L = 50/(0.5*40·0.0225) ≈ 111. With L=2, W=222.
* Use W=8 nf=2 L=1 → W/L = 16. Vov_p ≈ 250 mV. OK.
XM6     na     na     VDD    VDD  sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8  L=1 W=8 nf=2 m=1
XM7     nb     na     VDD    VDD  sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8  L=1 W=8 nf=2 m=1

* ---- Cascode bias voltages
* Vb1 = Vov_M1 + Vgs_M3 ≈ 0.18 + 0.85 = 1.03 V  (force M1 into saturation)
* Vb2 = nb - Vgs_M5 ≈ 1.55 - 1.05 = 0.50 V
VBIAS1  Vb1    VSS    dc 1.05
VBIAS2  Vb2    VSS    dc 0.50

.ends
